# No Emojis Rule

All AI agents must strictly avoid using emojis anywhere in this project.

## Guidelines

- **Zero Emojis**: Never insert or output emojis (Unicode emoji characters or pictographs) in code, comments, documentation, UI strings, logs, commit messages, or agent responses.
- **Text Alternatives**: Use standard plain-text status tags or descriptors instead of emoji icons (for example: `[OK]`, `[ERROR]`, `[WARNING]`, `[INFO]`, `[DONE]`, `[In Progress]`).
- **UI Icons**: In frontend components, use formal vector icon components (such as Lucide icons or standard SVGs) rather than Unicode emojis.

## Examples

### Logging and Console Output

```typescript
// Bad:
console.log("Initialization complete"); // with emoji
console.error("Failed to connect"); // with emoji

// Good:
console.log("[OK] Initialization complete");
console.error("[ERROR] Failed to connect");
```

### Documentation and Headings

```markdown
<!-- Bad: -->
## Features (with rocket or spark emoji)

<!-- Good: -->
## Features
```
